      "text": "PhNHCH $_{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4Cmuh",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{PhNH}_{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6PqBd",
      "text": "PhOH",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When primary amine react with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide, they produce - isocyamides as main product. The reaction is also known as carbyl amine reaction. $\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{CHCl}_{3}}{\\mathrm{KOH} \\text { (ethanolic) }} \\mathrm{Ph} \\cdot \\mathrm{N} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{C}$\r\n(Nauseating smell)",
    "image": null
  },
